## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.

1. On their line, press **Name**. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press **Save the name**.
2. The name shows on Visitors (Live now and History), the visit''s pages and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.
3. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.
4. Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours ("Booked"). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat''s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.
5. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Live map

A map of the Greater Toronto Area from Hamilton at the bottom to Barrie at the top, Toronto in the middle, with a dot for every lead, made for a TV or monitor in the office. It reads like a real map: every city and town is outlined (the GTA''s regions, Toronto, Peel, York, Durham, Halton and Hamilton, a little stronger), with the highways and the major roads, the cities'' names, a soft glow where people live and the Niagara Escarpment and the Oak Ridges Moraine as gentle ridges; the lake stays dark and quiet. A lead outside that area widens the map, keeping Toronto in the middle.

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**: the map is at the top. The four numbers: who is on the site now, requests today, cars on rent now and the money collected this month.
2. Each dot is one person, coloured by their stage: green on rent or booked, amber requests and forms (a request, a form sent or a form started), cyan on the site now or a game played, grey past renters. The stages under the map count each one; press one to hide or show it. Renters on rent, bookings and hot leads show as a small card with a photo of their car, framed in their stage colour (the make''s initial when the car has no photo); a hot lead not yet booked has a rose ring. Cards that would cover each other move apart, with a fine line back to their place. Each card and dot carries the person''s first name and last initial ("Visitor in Mississauga" when we do not know who it is). A visitor on the site breathes slowly, a new event sends one ripple, and crowded dots join in a count bubble, coloured by the hottest person in it (press it to zoom in until it splits; people on one spot open as a ring). Names show only for leads and hot visitors, from city zoom up, and pins are a little smaller at city zoom. Busy areas glow softly. The C marker is home base (the delivery origin in **Settings** > **Program**), with a thin line running to each car on rent or booked.
3. Rest the pointer on a lead (a dot or a car card), or move to it with Tab, to preview its card; press it to keep the card open (on a phone or tablet, tap it). The card shows the full name, the stage, the score from 0 to 100 with every signal, the car they looked at last with its photo and daily price, the city, how long they were on the site or when they were last seen, and a link to open the booking, the renter, Live visitors or Renter leads. Press × or Escape to close it. In the list under the map (Live now or History), press a visitor''s icon or **Show on the map** to bring them to the middle of the map with their card.
4. Phones and emails are hidden until you turn on **Show contact** (above the map, and at the top of the side panel in TV mode); the switch works for the map and for the list under it. The choice is remembered on that computer. While it is off, the page never receives them, so a TV left on holds none. Only Admins see them, as on the renter and lead pages.
5. Press **Open TV mode** on the computer connected to the TV and make the browser full screen (F11 on Windows, Control Command F on a Mac). The map fills the screen with the four numbers on top and the stages on On the road''s title line (no pin hides under the numbers or On the road); along the bottom, On the road: the cars on rent and those picked up today, with the renter and when the car is due back (a booking with no car yet shows Car not assigned); on the right, the hottest lead with the car''s photo and the signals that put them there (leads only: never someone on rent or booked; "No hot leads right now" when there is none; changing every 10 seconds) and the live feed, one line per event. Press a lead on the map, in the live feed or in On the road for its card; on the TV the card closes by itself after 20 seconds. It refreshes every 30 seconds and hides the pointer when the mouse is still.

- Where a dot goes: the approximate place of the visitor''s network (about 1 km, from Cloudflare), else the centre of the renter''s home city or of the visit''s city. Nothing is looked up and no address is shown. People with no place are counted under the map.
- The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.
- No hardware acceleration: when the browser has WebGL turned off (in Chrome, Settings > System > Use graphics acceleration when available), the same map is drawn another way, a little slower, and a note in the corner says so. Turning hardware acceleration on makes it faster.
- The fleet layer: once CarmaCars'' trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick **Fleet** to show or hide it.

## Past visits (History)

Press **History** under the map for the visits before now, in one list grouped by day (Today, Yesterday, then the date). Each visit is one row: the time, who (a name when we know it, with what they are to us: Owner, Owner · renter, Investor, Partner, Staff or Renter), the city, where they came from (ad, search, direct), the pages and small photos of the cars they looked at (up to 3 and "+n"), a dot for the score and what it led to (Request sent, Booked, Account, Lead, Chat or Left). Press a row for the pages in order, how long and where; **Open the visit** has every page and event, and **Show on the map** finds them there when they are still on it. Pick **Today**, **7 days**, **30 days** or **90 days** to set the dates in one press, or **Custom** to type them; the Source and Led to filters are next to the dates and **More filters** has the city, the device, the landing page, the country, new or returning, and bots and staff. The search box above the list narrows the rows on the page. One line shows the totals; **Day by day and top pages** opens the chart and the top lists. Visitor history and Live visitors are now this one page; their old links open it.

## The signals

Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.

- Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.
- Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a "near me" search.
- Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.
- Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.
- Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.

## Hot visitors and the actions

- When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.
- A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.
- Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.
- Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago") so two people do not write to the same visitor.

## Signal settings

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors** and press **Signal settings** (above the Live now list).
2. Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).
3. Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for "Pickup soon", 3 searches for "Searching dates again and again"), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.
4. Press **Save the signals**. The next look at each visit uses them.

## Follow-up tasks

Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours".

- An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.
- The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.
- A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.
- A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.
- The thresholds are in **Settings** > **Program**, group "Live visitors and live chat", with how long "on the site now" lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.

## Recovery emails

Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.

- An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.
- A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).
- Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).
- They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, "Booking recovery emails".

## Interest in a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, a car, Overview: "Interest on the site" shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has "Most viewed cars this week".

## A renter''s visits

On a renter''s page (People > Renters, the name) and on a booking''s Messages & history section, the Activity log (chip **Website**) lists each visit, when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, searched, the signals, and (chip **Live chat**) their chats line by line.

## Live chat

1. A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press **Open the chat**. Or open **Today** > **Visitors** and press the **Chat** tab (the old Live chat address opens it). The menu counts the chats that need a reply: a chat waiting for a person, or one a person has where the visitor wrote last. Live chat shows the same number. Those chats come first, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor''s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over**: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press **Send** (or Enter).
4. **Hand back to the assistant** lets it answer again. **Close** ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. **Email the transcript** sends it any time.
5. Alerts: each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert to the bell and, with phone alerts on, to your phone (topic Messages), on shift or not. A chat someone has goes to that person only. The alert clears when someone replies or the chat closes. "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" and desktop alerts in this browser are in Notify me.

> Tip: The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car''s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor''s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose "I sourced this client" on the quote or offer.

## When the visitor leaves

- A visitor not seen on the site for 10 minutes has left (Settings > Program, "Live chat: a visitor not seen on the site for this many minutes has left").
- No phone or email: the chat closes by itself, marked **Visitor left, no contact**. It leaves the count and its alerts clear.
- A phone or email (typed in the chat, left in the contact box, or on their renter account): the chat stays open as **Follow up by text/email**, out of the count, and customer service gets the task "Follow up by text/email" in their queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done.
- A visitor who comes back to the site opens the chat again where it was.

## When the assistant does not answer

The assistant answers first, within seconds, and asks for a phone number or email early so we can follow up. It hands over when the visitor asks for a person or when it is not sure.

- When it cannot answer, Live chat shows **AI replies paused** with the reason: turned off in Settings, today''s live share of the free AI allowance used, or the last reply failed. The chat goes to a person and the conversation shows a staff note (only staff see it).
- Common questions (the deposit, age and licence, how booking works, cancellation, hours, delivery) are answered from our own facts with no AI use.
- The free AI allowance is shared by tier (open **Settings**, then **Usage**): the staff assistant keeps 30%, live features (visitor chat, the phone line, the readers) have 50%, background writing 10%. Press **Change the shares** to change them.

## The assistant''s settings

In Program settings, "Live visitors and live chat": the chat on or off, the AI first or not (on by default), its model (Llama 3.1 8B), the neurons it may use a day (6,000, a few hundred replies; then chats wait for a person), when a visitor has left (10 minutes), the greeting on car pages after some seconds (off by default), how long chats and visits are kept, as the privacy policy says: chats 12 months, the pages of a visit 90 days, the visit''s summary in History 13 months, and the daily totals, which name no one, 3 years.

## What a visitor typed

A visitor who typed contact details into a form shows them on their line: "Typed into the booking request, not sent: Maya Chen, maya@example.com", with **Email not confirmed** until they open the link we emailed, and **Renter page**.


## Visitors for customer service and Sales

Customer service and Sales have the same Visitors page in their menu: the map with its clusters, Live now, Chat and History, the roles and Show contact. Their map has no fleet layer and no money figure; History opens a visit''s details in the list (the visit''s own page stays in Admin). The staff Live visitors and Live chat addresses open it.

## Signals that alert on their own (release 34)
Open Signal settings. Each signal has a box, Alert on its own. When it is ticked and that signal turns on in a visit, the Admins and the customer service and Sales staff on duty get an alert at once, without waiting for the visitor to turn Hot, once a visitor a day. It is ticked for Came back for the same car. Untick it to stop those alerts; the signal still counts towards the score.

## Working now and the leaderboard

The live map (and its TV mode) shows **Working now**: staff clocked in or on a field shift, with their role and since when, and **Sales this week**, the bookings credited to each salesperson. **On rent now** counts every booking on a trip, those whose pickup was never recorded included.',
  '<p class="gd-p">See who is on the site right now and what they look at, with buying signals, and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers the chat first; you take over whenever you want, and it hands over by itself for complaints, damage, payments and anything it should not answer.</p><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-visitors" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live visitors</h2><p class="gd-p">Visitors who accepted analytics (or got the notice in Canada outside Quebec and the US), known customers on their own booking pages and anyone in a chat.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b>. Three tabs sit on top: <b class="gd-ui">Live now</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> (live chat, with Texts and calls) and <b class="gd-ui">History</b>; the menu&#39;s count is the chats waiting plus the hot visitors. On Live now the map is at the top (see Live map below); under it, <b class="gd-ui">Live now</b> lists who is on the site now (seen in the last 5 minutes; an open page says it is still there every 45 seconds, so someone reading one page stays on the list), and <b class="gd-ui">History</b> the visits before (see Past visits below). The line at the top of Live now counts who is live, the visitors today (people, with their visits), hot visitors now, known customers now and chats today. The menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor has an icon for what they are doing (in a chat, a form sent or started, a known customer, on the site); a known person shows what they are to us (Owner, Owner · renter, Investor, Partner, Staff, Renter) from all their records, never just &quot;renter&quot; for an owner; press it, or <b class="gd-ui">Show on the map</b>, to see them on the map with their card. Filter the list by type, city and source.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Visitors who chose necessary cookies only are never recorded: a line under the counts says how many chose that today. Closing the tab takes a visitor off the list at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100, with Hot (60 or more), Warm (30 or more) or Cold. The list is sorted by it; choose &quot;Most recent&quot; in Sort, or tick &quot;Hot and warm only&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Why&quot; gives the three strongest reasons, for example &quot;Pickup tomorrow · Reached step 3 of the request form · Tapped to call&quot;. The badges are all the signals of the visit; the dots say how strong each is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each visitor also shows their name when known (signed in, or arrived from one of our emails), otherwise &quot;Visitor from Toronto, phone&quot;; the page and car they are on, and how many others look at that car now; the device, city, the site or campaign that sent them and &quot;from an ad&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Suggested: the best next step and the message to send. Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to chat with this message</b> to send it at once, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the message</b> to change it first, <b class="gd-ui">Offer a 10% discount code</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Assign to Sales</b> or, when their dates are taken, <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a similar free car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Pages</b> for every page and event of the visit with each signal&#39;s points, or <b class="gd-ui">Start a chat</b> to write your own message. They see it in a bubble and reply from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Below: hot visitors today (and whether someone acted), the signals of the last 24 hours, and the most viewed cars of the week with prices shown and the car most compared with each. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-name-a-visitor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Name a visitor</h2><p class="gd-p">When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On their line, press <b class="gd-ui">Name</b>. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the name</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The name shows on Visitors (Live now and History), the visit&#39;s pages and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours (&quot;Booked&quot;). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat&#39;s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit name</b> changes it; <b class="gd-ui">Remove the name</b> takes it off.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live map</h2><p class="gd-p">A map of the Greater Toronto Area from Hamilton at the bottom to Barrie at the top, Toronto in the middle, with a d