now&quot; when there is none; changing every 10 seconds) and the live feed, one line per event. Press a lead on the map, in the live feed or in On the road for its card; on the TV the card closes by itself after 20 seconds. It refreshes every 30 seconds and hides the pointer when the mouse is still.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Where a dot goes: the approximate place of the visitor&#39;s network (about 1 km, from Cloudflare), else the centre of the renter&#39;s home city or of the visit&#39;s city. Nothing is looked up and no address is shown. People with no place are counted under the map.</li><li>The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.</li><li>No hardware acceleration: when the browser has WebGL turned off (in Chrome, Settings &gt; System &gt; Use graphics acceleration when available), the same map is drawn another way, a little slower, and a note in the corner says so. Turning hardware acceleration on makes it faster.</li><li>The fleet layer: once CarmaCars&#39; trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> to show or hide it.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-past-visits-history" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Past visits (History)</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">History</b> under the map for the visits before now, in one list grouped by day (Today, Yesterday, then the date). Each visit is one row: the time, who (a name when we know it, with what they are to us: Owner, Owner · renter, Investor, Partner, Staff or Renter), the city, where they came from (ad, search, direct), the pages and small photos of the cars they looked at (up to 3 and &quot;+n&quot;), a dot for the score and what it led to (Request sent, Booked, Account, Lead, Chat or Left). Press a row for the pages in order, how long and where; <b class="gd-ui">Open the visit</b> has every page and event, and <b class="gd-ui">Show on the map</b> finds them there when they are still on it. Pick <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, <b class="gd-ui">7 days</b>, <b class="gd-ui">30 days</b> or <b class="gd-ui">90 days</b> to set the dates in one press, or <b class="gd-ui">Custom</b> to type them; the Source and Led to filters are next to the dates and <b class="gd-ui">More filters</b> has the city, the device, the landing page, the country, new or returning, and bots and staff. The search box above the list narrows the rows on the page. One line shows the totals; <b class="gd-ui">Day by day and top pages</b> opens the chart and the top lists. Visitor history and Live visitors are now this one page; their old links open it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-the-signals" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The signals</h2><p class="gd-p">Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.</li><li>Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a &quot;near me&quot; search.</li><li>Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.</li><li>Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.</li><li>Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-hot-visitors-and-the-actions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hot visitors and the actions</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.</li><li>A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.</li><li>Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.</li><li>Each action shows on the visitor (&quot;Invited by Lena, 2 min ago&quot;) so two people do not write to the same visitor.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-signal-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signal settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Signal settings</b> (above the Live now list).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for &quot;Pickup soon&quot;, 3 searches for &quot;Searching dates again and again&quot;), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the signals</b>. The next look at each visit uses them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-follow-up-tasks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Follow-up tasks</h2><p class="gd-p">Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example &quot;Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours&quot;.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.</li><li>The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.</li><li>A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.</li><li>A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.</li><li>The thresholds are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, group &quot;Live visitors and live chat&quot;, with how long &quot;on the site now&quot; lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-recovery-emails" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Recovery emails</h2><p class="gd-p">Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.</li><li>A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).</li><li>Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).</li><li>They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, &quot;Booking recovery emails&quot;.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-interest-in-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interest in a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, a car, Overview: &quot;Interest on the site&quot; shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has &quot;Most viewed cars this week&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-a-renter-s-visits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A renter&#39;s visits</h2><p class="gd-p">On a renter&#39;s page (People &gt; Renters, the name) and on a booking&#39;s Messages &amp; history section, the Activity log (chip <b class="gd-ui">Website</b>) lists each visit, when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, searched, the signals, and (chip <b class="gd-ui">Live chat</b>) their chats line by line.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-chat" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live chat</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>. Or open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> and press the <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> tab (the old Live chat address opens it). The menu counts the chats that need a reply: a chat waiting for a person, or one a person has where the visitor wrote last. Live chat shows the same number. Those chats come first, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor&#39;s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b>: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or Enter).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hand back to the assistant</b> lets it answer again. <b class="gd-ui">Close</b> ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. <b class="gd-ui">Email the transcript</b> sends it any time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Alerts: each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert to the bell and, with phone alerts on, to your phone (topic Messages), on shift or not. A chat someone has goes to that person only. The alert clears when someone replies or the chat closes. &quot;Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)&quot; and desktop alerts in this browser are in Notify me.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car&#39;s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor&#39;s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose &quot;I sourced this client&quot; on the quote or offer.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-when-the-visitor-leaves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When the visitor leaves</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A visitor not seen on the site for 10 minutes has left (Settings &gt; Program, &quot;Live chat: a visitor not seen on the site for this many minutes has left&quot;).</li><li>No phone or email: the chat closes by itself, marked <b class="gd-ui">Visitor left, no contact</b>. It leaves the count and its alerts clear.</li><li>A phone or email (typed in the chat, left in the contact box, or on their renter account): the chat stays open as <b class="gd-ui">Follow up by text/email</b>, out of the count, and customer service gets the task &quot;Follow up by text/email&quot; in their queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done.</li><li>A visitor who comes back to the site opens the chat again where it was.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-when-the-assistant-does-not-answer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When the assistant does not answer</h2><p class="gd-p">The assistant answers first, within seconds, and asks for a phone number or email early so we can follow up. It hands over when the visitor asks for a person or when it is not sure.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>When it cannot answer, Live chat shows <b class="gd-ui">AI replies paused</b> with the reason: turned off in Settings, today&#39;s live share of the free AI allowance used, or the last reply failed. The chat goes to a person and the conversation shows a staff note (only staff see it).</li><li>Common questions (the deposit, age and licence, how booking works, cancellation, hours, delivery) are answered from our own facts with no AI use.</li><li>The free AI allowance is shared by tier (open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Usage</b>): the staff assistant keeps 30%, live features (visitor chat, the phone line, the readers) have 50%, background writing 10%. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the shares</b> to change them.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-the-assistant-s-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The assistant&#39;s settings</h2><p class="gd-p">In Program settings, &quot;Live visitors and live chat&quot;: the chat on or off, the AI first or not (on by default), its model (Llama 3.1 8B), the neurons it may use a day (6,000, a few hundred replies; then chats wait for a person), when a visitor has left (10 minutes), the greeting on car pages after some seconds (off by default), how long chats and visits are kept, as the privacy policy says: chats 12 months, the pages of a visit 90 days, the visit&#39;s summary in History 13 months, and the daily totals, which name no one, 3 years.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-what-a-visitor-typed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What a visitor typed</h2><p class="gd-p">A visitor who typed contact details into a form shows them on their line: &quot;Typed into the booking request, not sent: Maya Chen, maya@example.com&quot;, with <b class="gd-ui">Email not confirmed</b> until they open the link we emailed, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter page</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-visitors-for-customer-service-and-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Visitors for customer service and Sales</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and Sales have the same Visitors page in their menu: the map with its clusters, Live now, Chat and History, the roles and Show contact. Their map has no fleet layer and no money figure; History opens a visit&#39;s details in the list (the visit&#39;s own page stays in Admin). The staff Live visitors and Live chat addresses open it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-signals-that-alert-on-their-own-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signals that alert on their own (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Signal settings. Each signal has a box, Alert on its own. When it is ticked and that signal turns on in a visit, the Admins and the customer service and Sales staff on duty get an alert at once, without waiting for the visitor to turn Hot, once a visitor a day. It is ticked for Came back for the same car. Untick it to stop those alerts; the signal still counts towards the score.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-working-now-and-the-leaderboard" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Working now and the leaderboard</h2><p class="gd-p">The live map (and its TV mode) shows <b class="gd-ui">Working now</b>: staff clocked in or on a field shift, with their role and since when, and <b class="gd-ui">Sales this week</b>, the bookings credited to each salesperson. <b class="gd-ui">On rent now</b> counts every booking on a trip, those whose pickup was never recorded included.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'chapter', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.

## The inbox

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.
2. Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo''s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.
3. Write a text and press **Send text**: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. **Suggest a reply** puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.
4. Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.
5. **Stop texts** stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. **Match automatically again** undoes a link made by hand.

## Missed calls

A missed call raises the task "Missed call from ..." for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.

> Tip: Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, "Missed call: text the caller back"), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo''s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.

## Calls and texts on records

A renter''s page and a booking''s Messages & history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips **Texts** and **Calls**); an owner''s page has "Calls and texts". Calls are not recorded on the line for now, so there is no transcript or recording to show.

## The Activity log (release 35)

A renter''s page and a booking''s **Messages & history** section have one **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking''s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.

1. **All** shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press **All** to go back.
2. Type in **Search the activity** and press **Search** to find a word in the log; **Clear** takes it away.
3. 50 lines show at a time: **Older** shows the next 50, **Newest** goes back to the top.
4. **Email**, **Call** and **Text** are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has **Reply**, a text or call from them **Text** or **Call**, a chat line **Open the chat**.
5. **Add a note** is above the log; the note shows in it at once.

> Good to know: Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking''s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.

## Quo contacts

Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.

- A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.
- One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.
- A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.
- If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.
- **Settings**, **Quo contacts**: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and **Sync everyone again**. Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)", turn it off.

## Booking texts

Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and **Settings**, **Text alerts**).

## The settings

Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)": the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Today** > **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls**; press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. To use the phone''s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** in **Settings** > **Program**. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.

## The CarmaCars app links

**Settings** > **Program**, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see **Download the CarmaCars app** in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.

## Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)

When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder''s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.

1. A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, **overdue** when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.
2. Write what the call was about in **Note about this call** and press **Add note**: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.
3. **Open the renter''s page** opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.
4. An unknown number shows **Unknown caller**: press **Create lead** to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.
5. Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).

## Renter notes (release 34)

Every renter page has **Add a note**, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip **Notes**): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press **Remove** and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter''s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal''s renter.

## The Call button through Twilio (release 35)
Quo keeps incoming calls, texts and AI answering. **Call** on a staff page rings the staff member''s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then **Call** opens Quo and says why.

Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, **Reveal** shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.
', 'Texts and calls (the Quo phone line)', 'Texts and calls in the chat inbox, unknown callers, missed calls, booking texts, call summaries and the settings.',
