ass="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. A short form opens: the <b class="gd-ui">Role</b> (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the <b class="gd-ui">Start date</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, filled in with the role&#39;s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm: hire and start onboarding</b>. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do&#39;s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email; their call slot and AI interview link close.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire&#39;s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Without a camera or a microphone they type, on the same clock. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript and the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">You decide, as after a call: the rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>. Or press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>: the candidate gets the link to book a video call (they wait for an interview day like everyone else).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The AI never hires or declines anyone: nothing goes to the candidate until you send the decision emails. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'your-workday', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.

## The menu

Every office role has the same short menu: **To do** (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one **More** for the rest of your work, **Bookings** (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and **Me** (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: **Send an offer** and **New quote** on Requests, **Add a rental** on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters'' phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.

A **More** page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.

| Function | Your links, then More |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur |
| Sales | Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur |
| Fleet | Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button) |
| Finance | Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills |

## To do

Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.

1. The top shows your function, today''s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.
2. **Next up** is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or **Take it** to make it yours.
3. Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.
4. Customer service and Sales: **Waiting for a reply** lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today''s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.
5. **Every open task**: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.
6. Press **Take it** to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. **Sheet** opens the step-by-step procedure.
7. Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day''s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.
8. On a computer, press **/** to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 48.6 20.2, 2 31.9 52.1, 3 41.7 72.3")

## Work a task

Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.

| Button | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Open the working screen** | Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about. |
| **Done** | You finished it. It leaves the queue. |
| **Waiting** | You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours. |
| **Escalate** | It needs an Admin. Add why. |
| **Hand over** | Give it to someone else on the team. |
| **Add a note** | Leave a note for whoever looks next. |

> Tip: Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.

## Today

1. Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.
2. Press a booking number to open it. **To do** takes you back to your tasks.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 700; address: carmacars.ca/va/today; pins: 1 22.9 24.6")

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. The queue shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Several functions? Switch with Working as

If you cover more than one function, **Working as** above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.

## Your scorecard

1. Open **Me** (the **Scorecard** tab).
2. By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.
4. The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 360; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 1 4.2 39.7, 2 62.5 58.3")
', 'Your workday', 'The menu, To do, task actions, Today, switching functions and your scorecard.',
